flowchart TB
  accTitle: Contract to runtime connection chain
  accDescr: Contract semantics are selected by a stable Anchor, implemented by a service-port binding, connected by a composition wire, and resolved to a runtime endpoint with an optional configuration materializer.

  subgraph Definition["Reusable DOT definition"]
    direction LR
    Contract["1 · Contract operation<br/>authoritative interaction facts"]
    Anchor["2 · Anchor<br/>stable UUID and role"]
    Binding["3 · Anchor binding<br/>service and named port"]
    Contract -->|selected by| Anchor
    Anchor -->|implemented by| Binding
  end

  subgraph Topology["Composition topology"]
    Wire["4 · Wire<br/>named DOT instances"]
  end

  subgraph Runtime["Deployment instance"]
    direction LR
    Endpoint["5 · Resolved endpoint<br/>host and allocated port"]
    Materializer["6 · Optional materializer<br/>declared receiver configuration"]
    Endpoint -.->|when required| Materializer
  end

  Definition -->|connected through| Topology
  Topology -->|resolved after deployment| Runtime

  classDef definition fill:#e8f2f7,stroke:#2b6777,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef topology fill:#eef6f3,stroke:#39826f,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef runtime fill:#f6f8fa,stroke:#687887,color:#17232d,stroke-width:1.5px;
  class Contract,Anchor,Binding definition;
  class Wire topology;
  class Endpoint,Materializer runtime;
